<h1>Week 29</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Lana</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> Erasure</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>The Circus</em></p>

<p>Kayla,</p>

<p>
I wasn’t planning on including this, but your last album and the song “Soco Amaretto Lime” made me think so much about Lisa and the fun times we had.
</p>

<p>
So I had to add this to my list for you:
</p>

<p>
<em>The Circus</em> by Erasure.
</p>

<p>
Erasure is a super synthy 80s duo. One of the guys was in Yaz and Depeche Mode.
</p>

<p>
The song “Sometimes” was really popular in the club and the reason I bought the cassette.
</p>

<p>
How this made my list for you is that the funnest night of my life had this as the soundtrack, not by choice.
</p>

<p>
Disclaimer: I wouldn’t recommend or condone my behavior.
</p>

<p>
Lisa and I took acid and went to Graffittis. It was way too much for us to stay because of the colors, strobe lights, and checkered floor. So we left.
</p>

<p>
Lisa normally was the driver in her Mazda RX7. I can picture it so clearly as I write this. Lisa was having trouble with her contacts, so at night she could only wear one.
</p>

<p>
So after a crazy, and I mean crazy, drive to our house, we switched to my car.
</p>

<p>
My stereo was broken, so all we had was the radio, which you now know meant shit music all night. But I risked it and switched to the cassette.
</p>

<p>
And like magic, for this night only, it worked.
</p>

<p>
This was what was in there. Not either of our favorites, but it became the soundtrack of our wild adventures that night.
</p>

<p>
We sang our hearts out and laughed until we cried and decided our crazy trip was actually another planet called Naeba.
</p>

<p>
I think our planet song was “Victim Of Love.” Lisa thinks it was “Sometimes,” so we decided to tell you it’s our planet’s album.
</p>

<p>
I hope you enjoy.
</p>

<p>
Again, closing with the disclaimer, I don’t recommend or condone this behavior. 🤣
</p>

<p>
I love you.
</p>

<p>
Mom
</p>

